          <compound>
            <id type="integer">644</id>
            <name>3-Phosphoglyceric acid</name>
            <hmdb-id>HMDB0000807</hmdb-id>
            <description>3-phosphoglyceric acid (3PG) is a 3-carbon molecule that is a metabolic intermediate in both glycolysis and the Calvin cycle. This chemical is often termed PGA when referring to the Calvin cycle. In the Calvin cycle, two glycerate 3-phosphate molecules are reduced to form two molecules of glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate (GALP). (wikipedia).</description>
